  "description": "Provisions AlloyDB Express clusters and 1-vCPU ZONAL primary instances for rapid, low-cost non-production PostgreSQL 18 workloads over Private Service Connect (PSC) or Public DNS, with scale-to-zero cost optimization. Use when the user asks to spin up a quick prototype, build a proof of concept (POC), try out a feature in a sandbox, or set up a development or staging AlloyDB database while minimizing compute costs or avoiding an always-on cluster. Don't use for production workloads requiring REGIONAL availability type, read pools, continuous backup or point-in-time recovery, CMEK, VPC peering, instances over 2 vCPUs, storage over 20 GB, inspecting existing clusters or instances, or querying and indexing tables.",
